From: opencode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:20:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ORBIS: FindFFmpeg never searches host default include paths

On Linux hosts find_path() fell back to the host's /usr/include, so the
FFmpeg targets carried -isystem /usr/include ahead of the SDK paths: that
flipped <stdint.h> to glibc's and broke orbis_prefix.h under the SDK's musl
sysroot (bits/libc-header-start.h not found). With NO_DEFAULT_PATH the
lookup is constrained to the paths that were already listed (the FFmpeg
dir passes everything the port needs).

Co-Authored-By: opencode (Claude, sandbox do usuario)
---
 CMakeModules/find/FindFFmpeg.cmake | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeModules/find/FindFFmpeg.cmake b/CMakeModules/find/FindFFmpeg.cmake
index 11dd08a..d679b9b 100644
--- a/CMakeModules/find/FindFFmpeg.cmake
+++ b/CMakeModules/find/FindFFmpeg.cmake
@@ -93,10 +93,12 @@ function(find_ffmpeg LIBNAME)
 
   find_path(FFmpeg_INCLUDE_${LIBNAME} lib${LIBNAME}/${LIBNAME}.h
     HINTS ${INCLUDE_PATHS}
+    NO_DEFAULT_PATH NO_CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH
   )
 
   find_library(FFmpeg_LIBRARY_${LIBNAME} ${LIBNAME}
     HINTS ${LIB_PATHS}
+    NO_DEFAULT_PATH NO_CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH
   )
 
   if(NOT FFMPEG_DIR AND (NOT FFmpeg_LIBRARY_${LIBNAME} OR NOT FFmpeg_INCLUDE_${LIBNAME}))
